    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.harmonic_centrality - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.harmonic_centrality.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.harmonic_centrality()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Calculate harmonic centrality scores for all nodes.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.harmonic_centrality()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Calculate harmonic centrality scores for all nodes.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.harmonic_centrality()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Calculate harmonic centrality scores for all nodes.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nCalculate harmonic centrality scores for all nodes.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L52921-L53076){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.harmonic_centrality(\n    mode=\"out\",\n    normalized=False,\n    cutoff=None,\n    weighted=None,\n    attr_name=None,\n    return_dict=False,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Harmonic centrality](../assets/graphs/harmonic-centrality.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"The shared seven-node graph shaded by harmonic centrality, the sum of 1 over the distance to every other node. Hub C is closest to everyone and scores 4.83, followed by E 4.50, D 4.33 and B 4.08, while the pendant node G is palest.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nHarmonic centrality is the sum of the reciprocal of shortest path distances from a node to\nall other reachable nodes. For unreachable nodes, the distance is considered infinite, and\nthe reciprocal is `0`. This makes harmonic centrality more robust than closeness centrality\nfor disconnected graphs.\n\nThe formula is: `H(v) = Σ 1 / d(v,u)` for all `u ≠ v`, where `d(v,u)` is the shortest path\ndistance from `v` to `u`: the total edge weight on a weighted graph\n(`Graph(weighted=True)`), the number of hops otherwise.\n\nWhen `normalized=True`, the result is divided by `(n - 1)`, giving the mean inverse\ndistance, which is bounded between `0` and `1`.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[mode]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[&quot;out&quot;]{.st}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Direction for measuring distances in directed graphs where: (1) `\"out\"` follows edges in\n    their direction (default), (2) `\"in\"` follows edges in reverse, and (3) `\"all\"` or\n    `\"total\"` ignores edge directions (only for undirected graphs).\n\n<code>[normalized]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[False]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True`, divides by `(n - 1)` to normalize scores to the `[0, 1]` range. If `False`\n    (the default), returns raw sum of inverse distances.\n\n<code>[cutoff]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Maximum path length to consider (in hops, or in total weight when weights are used).\n    Paths longer than `cutoff=` are ignored. If `None` (default), there is no limit.\n\n<code>[weighted]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Whether to measure distances by edge weight. If `None` (default), follows the graph:\n    weights are used on a weighted graph (`Graph(weighted=True)`) and hop counts\n    otherwise, the same rule `shortest_path()` uses. Pass `True` or `False` to override.\n    Edges without a weight count as `1.0`; weights must be non-negative.\n\n<code>[attr_name]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [str | None]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Column name to store harmonic centrality scores in the node DataFrame. If `None`\n    (default), automatically uses 'harmonic_centrality'. Overwrites column if it already\n    exists.\n\n<code>[return_dict]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[False]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True`, returns dictionary instead of self. If `False` (default), stores in NDF and\n    returns self for chaining.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Union[dict[int, float], Graph]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `return_dict=` is `True`: dictionary mapping node IDs to harmonic centrality scores.\n    If `return_dict=` is `False` (the default): returns self for method chaining.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~closeness_centrality`) \n\n:   The reciprocal of the average distance.\n\n[](`~local_reaching_centrality`) \n\n:   The share of nodes a node can reach.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nOn a path, each node adds `1 / d` for every other node at distance `d`. The end nodes\nscore `1 + 1/2 + 1/3`, and `normalized=True` divides by the `n - 1 = 3` other nodes:\n\n::: {#2fc40b58 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\npath = ec.Graph.from_edges([(\"A\", \"B\"), (\"B\", \"C\"), (\"C\", \"D\")])\n\n(\n    path.harmonic_centrality()\n    .harmonic_centrality(normalized=True, attr_name=\"normalized\")\n    .get_node_df()\n    .select(\"label\", \"harmonic_centrality\", \"normalized\")\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```{=html}\n<div><style>\n.dataframe > thead > tr,\n.dataframe > tbody > tr {\n  text-align: right;\n  white-space: pre-wrap;\n}\n</style>\n<small>shape: (4, 3)</small><table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\"><thead><tr><th>label</th><th>harmonic_centrality</th><th>normalized</th></tr><tr><td>str</td><td>f64</td><td>f64</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>&quot;A&quot;</td><td>1.833333</td><td>0.611111</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;B&quot;</td><td>2.5</td><td>0.833333</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;C&quot;</td><td>2.5</td><td>0.833333</td></tr><tr><td>&quot;D&quot;</td><td>1.833333</td><td>0.611111</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Travel times on the metro\n\nThe metro is weighted by travel time, so here each station adds `1 / minutes` for every\nother station. Central, a few minutes from most of the network, scores highest, and the\nAirport, at the end of a long run, lowest:\n\n::: {#eb1f5c99 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nmetro = ec.metro().harmonic_centrality()\n\nmetro.plot(layout=\"pos\", color_by=\"harmonic_centrality\", label_by=\"label\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:c